        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "const u = $('Find User').first().json;\n\nfunction parseArr(v) {\n  if (v === null || v === undefined || v === '') return [];\n  if (Array.isArray(v)) return v;\n  try {\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(v);\n    return Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : [];\n  } catch (e) {\n    return [];\n  }\n}\n\nconst targetRoles = parseArr(u.target_roles_json);\n\nconst profile = {\n  id: u.auth_user_id ?? null,\n  first_name: u.first_name ?? null,\n  last_name: u.last_name ?? null,\n  email: u.email ?? null,\n  location: u.location ?? null,\n  country: u.country ?? null,\n  // \"Position of interest\" — the roles the user targets\n  positions_of_interest: targetRoles,\n  position_of_interest: targetRoles.length ? targetRoles[0] : null,\n  // Resume: only the extracted text is stored. No PDF file/URL exists yet.\n  resume: {\n    text: u.cv_text ?? null,\n    file_url: null,\n    file_name: null,\n  },\n};\n\nreturn [{ json: { success: true, profile } }];"
